{"id": "EUVD-2026-86712", "enisaUuid": "ea8bc596-2480-301d-9698-cbb22f75241b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark sched_process_wait argument as nullable\n\ndo_wait() passes wo->wo_pid to the sched_process_wait tracepoint.\nkernel_wait4() leaves wo_pid NULL for wait4(-1), and\nkernel_waitid_prepare() does likewise for waitid(P_ALL).\n\nbtf_ctx_access() currently types argument 0 as PTR_TO_BTF_ID |\nPTR_TRUSTED. Without PTR_MAYBE_NULL, the verifier accepts an unchecked\ndereference. Trusted pointer loads have no fault protection, so a wait for\nany child can then cause a NULL pointer dereference in JITed BPF code.\n\nAdd sched_process_wait to raw_tp_null_args[] with argument 0 marked\nnullable. The verifier rejects an unchecked dereference while preserving\naccess after the program checks the pointer for NULL.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:13:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bee862c79cb7e0e5c33b2df2e3a31d164705120d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c03a1b8ded858685a73c1ba4080adef99db4544", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9205e936dde9a94e93376c8de6195b740bcd5d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a453d6e3b8e8e1a321c8744d6189d763af9287d0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98059", "GHSA-mfrq-h74g-92w2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "020c3c92-579c-3fd3-a6c1-74324f70b823", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "16f469b2-376a-3d34-ac1d-abb107248eec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b2fc4b17fc13810ef440fb323fad3981cd174985 <bee862c79cb7e0e5c33b2df2e3a31d164705120d"}, {"id": "3a4b90f5-c336-3fcc-94a0-860139a75895", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "52f17c55-2288-3e66-8607-0f331972e0ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6ce37d4e-9d7c-3481-bfd4-9afd219fff98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "838a10bd2ebfe11a60dd67687533a7cfc220cc86 <b9205e936dde9a94e93376c8de6195b740bcd5d2"}, {"id": "80a623a4-87ef-3a6d-b35e-514645c39e90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "83cac5c6-af23-3dbe-973e-8fc5f8876317", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "adec6a34-0136-3df1-8fb0-2c49150543a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "838a10bd2ebfe11a60dd67687533a7cfc220cc86 <a453d6e3b8e8e1a321c8744d6189d763af9287d0"}, {"id": "c0606266-436d-3b48-a4ac-05fdfc50da75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "d722c12c-0a97-3b11-853a-ddd6e48bedd8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "838a10bd2ebfe11a60dd67687533a7cfc220cc86 <3c03a1b8ded858685a73c1ba4080adef99db4544"}, {"id": "e52f3ddf-f1cb-3b3a-8f02-f2a25f1d50b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.6 <6.12.111"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b1e331b8-5c2a-3e8e-b7e5-e9fd9f7d9ee1", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}